course: dictionary
lesson: 14920
title: Refrain: stop yourself, or a song's chorus
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Refrain can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, to refrain means to stop yourself from doing something. «Please refrain from talking in the library.» This is a polite, formal way of saying "please don't talk".
explain: As a noun, a refrain is the part of a song or poem that comes back again and again, like the chorus. «Everyone joined in on the refrain, the line they all knew by heart.» The clue is the song or poem around the word.
explain: Context tells you which job the word is doing. If refrain is followed by from and a doing word, it is the verb. If it sits inside a song or poem, it is probably the noun. A refrain can also be a comment people keep repeating: «Her familiar refrain was, "Tidy your room!"»
fact: Refrain can be a verb or a noun.
fact: To refrain from doing something means to hold yourself back from doing it.
fact: «Please refrain from running in the corridor» means please do not run in the corridor.
fact: A refrain is a line or lines that are repeated, like the chorus of a song.
fact: «A familiar refrain» means a comment or complaint that people keep hearing again and again.
exercise: «Please refrain from eating in the library.» What does refrain mean here? | Start a new game | *Stop yourself from doing something | Run very fast | Sing a loud song
exercise: «The whole class sang the refrain together.» What is a refrain? | A rule about where to sit | A type of musical instrument | *The part of a song that is repeated, the chorus | A long poem about the sea
exercise: Mum always says, «Tidy your room!» It is her familiar refrain. What does familiar refrain mean? | *A comment people keep repeating | A loud shout from the garden | A quick walk around the block | A new song she has just learned
test: What does refrain mean in «Please refrain from shouting in the hall»? | Repeat | Shout | *Avoid | Begin
test: What is the refrain in «The poem's refrain comes back after every verse»? | A verse | A question | *The repeated line | The title
exam: What job does refrain do in «The children must refrain from running in the hall»? | *A verb: it means to stop yourself from doing something | A name for a school | A type of game | A noun: it is the chorus of a song
